From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RCT Screensaver <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:33:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Title screen: import the next park into a second game state

The background load now also imports the park into a GameState_t of its
own: getGameState() and the map's tile index honor a thread-local
override while the loader thread imports, so the import code runs
unchanged against the staging state while the main thread keeps playing
the current park. On completion the main thread registers the objects,
swaps the game state and tile index in (swapGameState was unused), and
redoes the parts of the import that touch state outside GameState_t:
window intents, palette, animation and patrol caches, research flags,
plugin storage, the peep animation conversion of old parks, and the
post-import fix-ups (gameStateInitGlobals, IParkImporter::FinishImport).

Viewport and window invalidation and intents are no-ops on the loader
thread.
